#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Stage/adopt/check/activate the local source NVK + Rust RM stack for Waydroid.

Build the driver first (packaging/native/build-native.sh). Staging runs the source-native
regression gate on the exact build/ bytes it copies and stamps the manifest
(format 2) with that gate and the NVIDIA kernel module it ran on; the LXC
generator refuses any other module. No NVIDIA userspace enters the tree.
Activation requires a stopped container and saves the old config.

  stage-release BUNDLE DEST
                          developer tool: gate a CI-built release BUNDLE into a dev-root (packaged installs get the
                          vendor image instead: waydroid-nvidia-setup, packaging/native/vendor_image.py): hash-check
                          the CI-built release BUNDLE
                          (packaging/native/collect.py layout), run its install-time gate on this GPU and
                          kernel module (packaging/native/release_gate.py: CI-built programs, bionic runtime
                          from the user's system.img, logs in /var/lib/waydroid-nvidia), write format 3 to DEST
  stage DEST [--no-media REASON] [--no-native-gl REASON] [--nvrm-suffix SFX]
                          gate build/ (Vulkan regression gate + media gate + native GL gate), copy
                          it to the new DEST, write format 3. Media (Codec2 NVDEC decoder) is staged
                          unless explicitly opted out with a reason recorded in the manifest. Our
                          own GLES driver nvrm is staged (debug-stripped) when build/nvrm-android{,32}<SFX>
                          exist and pass the bionic smoke test on the staged bytes with NVK's
                          libnv_bionic_native.so; not built -> recorded as not staged
  adopt ROOT [--dry-run]  gate an existing format-1 ROOT whose artifacts equal build/
  check [ROOT] [--active] generator + (with --active) live-config checks
  status [ROOT]           health report, PASS/FAIL/UNKNOWN per line (normal user)
  activate ROOT           point /var/lib/waydroid/nvidia-prolapse at ROOT, select nvidia-prolapse with
                          nvidia_prolapse_install = dev-root in waydroid.cfg, systemd drop-in + pacman hook (root)
  install-hook            (re)write the pacman hook override only (root)
  hook                    pacman PostTransaction entry point; never fails
  restore BACKUP          return to a configuration saved by activate (root)
  invalidate-caches DIR   move obsolete HWUI/EGL shader caches into DIR (root)

check/status default to the nvidia-prolapse root link (/var/lib/waydroid/nvidia-prolapse).

A checkout runs the patched Waydroid it builds (build/waydroid, dev/build-waydroid). A packaged install
(the file PACKAGED next to dev/, written by packaging/native/install-native.sh) runs the system Waydroid
the package installed with the same patches, and refuses one whose generator differs from its own.
"""
